@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #4338CA
  FontColor #111827
}

title Concretizing a process as an LTS, so a μ-calculus predicate can be decided against it

' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' The concretization spine, left-to-right: a process term is given a one-step
' successor relation (HostTerm), unfolded into a finite reachable LTS
' (build_lts), model-checked by fixpoint iteration (denote), and the root's
' membership in ⟦φ⟧ is the decided predicate.
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
rectangle "a process term t\n(the thing to predicate)" as T #DBEAFE
component "HostTerm\nsuccessors(t): one-step labeled edges\nlabel(t): atomic proposition" as HT #CCFBF1
component "build_lts: BFS from t\nthe complete finite reachable LTS (S, →)\nuntil the frontier is empty" as BL #CCFBF1
component "denote: μ-calculus model check\n⟦φ⟧ ⊆ S by fixpoint iteration" as DN #FEF3C7
rectangle "evaluate(φ, t) = (root ∈ ⟦φ⟧)\nthe predicate decided in the behavioral Heyting algebra" as EV #DCFCE7

T --> HT : term to predicate
HT --> BL : one-step relation
BL --> DN : finite reachable LTS
DN --> EV : root membership

note bottom of BL #FEF3C7
  no implicit truncation: missing edges can make [a]φ vacuously true.
end note

note bottom of DN #E0E7FF
  modal satisfiability is DontKnow (semi-decidable); model-checking a GIVEN
  term is exact — the Heyting tier.
end note

legend right
|= Color |= Stage |
|<#DBEAFE> | the classical / exact input: a concrete process term t |
|<#CCFBF1> | LTS / automaton construction (HostTerm + build_lts) |
|<#FEF3C7> | μ-calculus model check by fixpoint iteration (semi-decidable family, exact on a given LTS) |
|<#DCFCE7> | the decided predicate (root ∈ ⟦φ⟧) in the behavioral Heyting algebra |
endlegend
@enduml
